menu "airmidi board"

    choice AIRMIDI_BOARD
        prompt "Board"
        default AIRMIDI_BOARD_XIAO_C6 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
        default AIRMIDI_BOARD_XIAO_S3 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        help
            The receiver PCB (rev A) with the XIAO module it carries. Selects the pin table and the board init.

        config AIRMIDI_BOARD_XIAO_C6
            bool "receiver rev A + XIAO ESP32-C6"
            depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6

        config AIRMIDI_BOARD_XIAO_S3
            bool "receiver rev A + XIAO ESP32-S3"
            depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3

        config AIRMIDI_BOARD_DEVKITC_S3
            bool "ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 on its own"
            depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
            help
                A bare dev kit on its native USB port: USB MIDI, the radios and the web UI, no TRS jacks wired
                (UART MIDI on GPIO17/18 if you add them), no battery, the BOOT button as the box's button.

        config AIRMIDI_BOARD_DIRECT_S3
            bool "Bare ESP32-S3 with a TRS port of its own"
            depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
            help
                A bare ESP32-S3 on a board of its own, with the TRS port hanging straight off two pins, each
                through a 22 ohm series resistor: TIP on the S3's GPIO14 and RING on the S3's GPIO15. A TRS port's
                type is which of the two carries the data, so holding the RING high and running the UART on the TIP
                is Type A, which is what the firmware does. Type B (the two pins swapped) is pending. The input is a
                6N137 optocoupler on the S3's GPIO21.
    endchoice

endmenu
